    <briefdescription>
<para>This class represents success/failure for parsing-like operations that find it important to chain together failable operations with <computeroutput>||</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is an extended version of <computeroutput><ref refid="structllvm_1_1_logical_result" kindref="compound">LogicalResult</ref></computeroutput> that allows for explicit conversion to bool.</para>
<para>This class should not be used for general error handling cases - we prefer to keep the logic explicit with the <computeroutput>succeeded</computeroutput>/<computeroutput>failed</computeroutput> predicates. However, traditional monadic-style parsing logic can sometimes get swallowed up in boilerplate without this, so we provide this for narrow cases where it is important. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
